From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] appxdeploymentclient: packages with external location, IPackageManager7-9 (6028)

TeraCopy's installer (and Advanced Installer's, and the Win11 context
menus of many programs) registers a "sparse" package: an MSIX of just a
manifest and assets whose program is in the installation folder, added
with IPackageManager9.AddPackageByUriAsync and
AddPackageOptions.ExternalLocationUri. Wine had neither the interface
nor the option classes, so the registration failed and the program had
no Start menu entry.

IPackageManager7 (RequestAddPackageAsync with packages to install),
IPackageManager8 (DeprovisionPackageForAllUsersAsync), IPackageManager9
(FindProvisionedPackages, Add/Stage/RegisterPackageByUriAsync,
RegisterPackagesByFullNameAsync, the stub preference);
AddPackageOptions, StagePackageOptions and RegisterPackageOptions.
A package's external location is recorded (ExternalLocation); its
applications' shortcuts and aliases start the programs there, and a
program there whose own manifest names the package (its msix element)
has the package's identity (kernelbase, ntdll's package graph). A
location for a package without uap10:AllowExternalContent is refused
(ERROR_PACKAGE_EXTERNAL_LOCATION_NOT_ALLOWED). AllowUnsigned installs
an unsigned package of the unsigned-publisher namespace and refuses one
outside it (and a signed one inside it). PackageVolume's Find* give
vectors of the packages. WindowsApps is in the machine's own Program
Files for a 32-bit caller too.
